            "Piping designers reconcile this trade in the system curve: short, heavily fitted branches are dominated by fitting losses, so the fixes are larger diameters, fewer bends and full-bore valves rather than a bigger pump. Field measurements usually show minor losses larger than predicted, which is why commissioning includes a measured head against flow at design point.",
