            "Press shops keep a tonnage table for this reason, and the practical design rule is to leave headroom above the calculated force because a worn tool, a thicker coil or a harder heat can push the peak upward. The same arithmetic sets the capacity of the die cushion and the frame stiffness that keeps the punch aligned.",
